      "content": "I can expand the guide significantly to meet the word count requirements. Here's the revised guide:\n\n**VPN Connection Timeout Error Troubleshooting Guide**\n\nA \"VPN Connection Timeout\" error occurs when your application takes too long to establish a secure connection with the VPN server, causing the entire process to time out and fail. This can be frustrating for users, leading to a poor remote access experience. To troubleshoot and resolve common causes of a \"VPN Connection Timeout\" error, follow these steps, carefully examining each component of the VPN connection process.\n\n**Step 1: Check VPN Server Health**\n\n1.1 Ensure the VPN server is operating within normal parameters. This is crucial, as a malfunctioning VPN server can significantly impact performance and cause connection timeouts. Before initiating a Remote Access session, review the VPN server's system requirements to ensure they match the client's system specifications.\n\n1.2 Verify the VPN server's DNS settings are correctly configured. DNS (Domain Name System) translates the client's hostname into an IP address that can be used to establish a secure connection with the VPN server. A poorly configured DNS can lead to temporary IP addresses or misconfigured server names, resulting in connection timeouts.\n\n1.3 Confirm that the VPN server's time is synchronized",
